## Context

Child of 0700, feeds 0704 (controversies 1 and 2). The OECD Rio / CRDF set,
recipient point of view, on which most effectiveness studies rest, is not a
homogeneous series:

- before 2013, the MDBs (IBRD, IDA, IFC, AfDB, EIB…) and the GEF do not appear
  in it; the CIFs enter in 2012, the GCF in 2015, the adaptation marker in 2010;
- two counting rules coexist: Rio markers at face value, MDB climate
  components.

Studies that stop around 2017 (Gavard & Schoch, 2000–2017) therefore mainly
measure a change of reporting around 2013. For the REL review, we present the
data, the evidence and the models on a consistently reconstructed series.
**This work belongs to REL, not to the Gavard & Schoch comment**, which sticks
to the published paper.

## Relevant files

- `~/CNRS/papiers/actif/Gavard Scotch 2026 Climate finance counterproductive/audit/`,
  outside the repo: `provider-check-2026-09-23/` (finding), `provider-sensitivity-2026-09-23/run.py`
  (provider-by-provider reconstruction method),
  `climate-finance-composition-2026-09-23/` (OECD vintage 2026, 2000–2017, in `raw/`).
- 0828 (feasibility of a CRS warehouse by agency): do not duplicate the CRS ingestion.

## Actions

1. **Fill the pre-2013 gap**: World Bank climate co-benefits by project
   (from about fiscal year 2011, to be checked); GEF project database;
   Climate Funds Update for dedicated funds; joint MDB reports (aggregates
   only). Document what remains impossible to fill.
2. **Extend after 2017**: most recent CRDF vintage; note the changes in OECD
   accounting rules and the rise of post-Paris flows.
3. Build a constant-provider-coverage series and a complete series, with the
   two counting rules kept separate.
4. Present in REL: data, evidence (breaks, composition), and models (what
   changes in the effectiveness results when the measure is consistent).

## Invariants

- The scope agreed with the editor (0700): the models part sticks to showing
  the sensitivity of the published conclusions to the measure; no new
  empirical study without talking to the editor again.
- EDM discipline and workpackage separation: data and scripts on the analysis
  side, the manuscript consumes artifacts.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Gap-filling sources inventoried, coverage by year documented
- [ ] Consistent series and complete series built, reproducible
- [ ] REL section (data, evidence, models) written
